-- title:
--   Drinfeld chart with Hasse datum at a supersingular stalk
-- statement:
--   Let $q \ge 5$ and $\ell \ge 3$ be primes with $\ell \ne q$, let $M' \ne 0$ be divisible by neither $q$ nor $\ell$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of level $q\ell$, and let $\zeta, \xi \in L$ be primitive $q$-th and $q\ell$-th roots of unity. Let $K \subset \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ be the intermediate field [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2 * M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) for the subgroup [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) of $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times$, namely the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$; thus $K$ is the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of that field of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant. Consider $\mathfrak{X} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra of elements integral over $A[j^{-1}]$. Let $z \in \mathfrak{X}$ be such that the germ at $z$ of $\varpi$, pulled back along the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and let $y$ be a point of the finite chart $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin` mapping to $z$, assumed supersingular in the sense that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic Weierstrass curves over $\Omega$ have no nonzero $q$-torsion point. The conclusion asserts the existence of a complete discrete valuation domain $W$ (adically complete for its maximal ideal), a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with maximal ideal of $W$ generated by $\sigma\varpi$, power series $f, u, v \in W[\![X_0, X_1]\!]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ at its maximal ideal onto $S = W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/(C(\sigma\varpi)v - fu)$, such that: (i) for every $a \in A$, $e$ sends the image in the completion of the germ at $z$ of $a$ to the class of the constant $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) every element $x$ of the residue field of $W$ satisfies $x^{q^n} = x$ for some $n \ge 1$; and (iii) the Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in `chartAlgFin`, and for that element there are $a_0 \in W$, $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e$ of the image of its germ at $z$ minus the class of $C(a_0)$ equal to the class of $h$, and with the degree-$e_0$ form of $h$ nondegenerate in the Hasse sense: for all $a, b \in W$ of which at least one is a unit and with $a^qb - ab^q$ in the maximal ideal, $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} h_{(i,\,e_0-i)}\,a^i b^{e_0-i}$ is a unit of $W$.
--
--   This is the existence half of the Drinfeld-chart analysis of the integral model at a supersingular point in characteristic $q$: the completed stalk is presented as a quotient of a two-variable power series ring over a complete discrete valuation ring in which the deformation equation agrees with the Drinfeld form $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ to order $q+2$, and the germ of the level-$q\ell$ $j$-series differs from a constant by a series whose leading form is a nondegenerate Hasse-type form. It is invoked to propagate the same Hasse datum from this one witness to an arbitrary Drinfeld presentation of the completed stalk.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevel_exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_const_residueField_pow_hasse_of_mem_ssJSet.lean

